:: Echo Fork
(set: $thud_lvl to 3)
Beyond the portcullis, the passage splits into rough-cut tunnels that all look the same. The heartbeat echoes off every surface.

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

(if: ($has: "heartstone"))[The Heartstone glows brightest when you face the portcullis.]\
(else:)[From the left tunnel, the beat comes softly, smothered by stone. From the right tunnel, it rings sharp and close.]

[[Take the left tunnel->Echo Bend]]
[[Take the right tunnel->Echo Door]]
[[Back under the portcullis->Weighing Room]]


:: Echo Bend
(set: $thud_lvl to 2)
The tunnel bends and narrows. The heartbeat is quieter here.

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

(if: ($has: "heartstone"))[The Heartstone dims in your hand. This is the wrong way.]\
(else:)[Ahead, the beat fades further still.]

[[Press on->Echo Hollow]]
[[Go back->Echo Fork]]


:: Echo Hollow
(set: $thud_lvl to 1)
A low, dead-end hollow. The heartbeat is barely a murmur. A crack in the far wall curls back the way you came.

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

[[Squeeze through the crack->Echo Fork]]
[[Go back->Echo Bend]]


:: Echo Door
(set: $thud_lvl to 4)
The tunnel ends at a stone edifice set with a worn [wooden door]<wooden|. Dull red light leaks from beneath it.
(click: ?wooden)[On closer inspection, the door has many thin spindle patterns inlaid in the wood. It once had a lacquer finish and a golden handle, but has since decayed from misuse.]

(display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

(if: ($has: "heartstone"))[The Heartstone flares when you face the tunnel behind you.]
<!-- (cycling-link: bind) resets the variable to its first string on every render, so each dial's
     list must start at its current value, or the dials reset whenever the player returns.
     (rotated:) can't do this: it rejects a rotation of 0. -->\
|heartdoor>[(set: _from to (dm:
	"moon", (a: "moon", "wave", "root", "flame"),
	"wave", (a: "wave", "root", "flame", "moon"),
	"root", (a: "root", "flame", "moon", "wave"),
	"flame", (a: "flame", "moon", "wave", "root"),
))\
(if: not $heart_door_open)[Three brass dials are set into the door, each engraved with a moon, a wave, a root, and a flame.

First dial: |dial1>[(cycling-link: bind $dial1, ...(_from's ($dial1)))]
Second dial: |dial2>[(cycling-link: bind $dial2, ...(_from's ($dial2)))]
Third dial: |dial3>[(cycling-link: bind $dial3, ...(_from's ($dial3)))]

(link-repeat: "Push the door")[(replace: ?heartdoorresult)[(if: $dial1 is "wave" and $dial2 is "root" and $dial3 is "flame")[(set: $heart_door_open to true)The dials click into place, and the door swings inward.](else:)[The door holds fast.](rerun: ?heartdoor)]]]\
(else:)[The wooden door stands open. [[Open the door.->Heart Chamber]]]]
|heartdoorresult>[]

[[Back down the tunnel->Echo Fork]]


:: Heart Chamber
(set: $thud_lvl to 4)
Behind the door is a small antechamber with rough-hewn stone covering the walls and floor. In each corner is a \
sconce with a luminous crystal casting red light across the floor.

(if: $where's heartstone is "Heart Chamber")[\
  In the center is a stone pedestal with a fist-sized blood red gem. Its facets seem to shift and \
  reverberate with the sound.

  (display: "CurrentSoundMsg")

  Take the Heartstone\
]<heartstone|\
(else:)[\
  (display: "CurrentSoundMsg")
]
[[Flee->Echo Door]]\

(click: "Take the Heartstone")[\
  <script>pushEvent('Story', 'Heartstone', 'Take')</script>\
  ($move: "heartstone", "player")\
  (set: $collapsing to true)(forget-undos: -1)(replace: ?sidebar)[]\
  (replace: ?heartstone)[\
    ---
    The gem feels heavy, and warm in your hand. It seems to jostle and shake of its own accord.

    Suddenly, the pulse quickens, slamming your mind with incessant pressure. Somewhere far behind you, the crawlway collapses with a roar. You must leave!

    (display: "CurrentSoundMsg")
  ]\
]
